 "result": "Only one failing test is outside the main root cause.\n\n- **`tests/test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`** is the only independent failure. It raises `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra in order to use async views` at `src/tessel/app.py:1096`, because the optional `asgiref` dependency isn't installed. Upgrading Werkzeug would not fix it.\n\nTwo other tests only look separate:\n\n- **`tests/test_request.py::test_limit_config`** is still the old-Werkzeug problem, with a different symptom. `max_form_memory_size` comes back `None` instead of 500_000 because Werkzeug 3.0.3 lacks that attribute, which was added in 3.1. I counted it separately only because the traceback differs from the `set_cookie` one.\n- **`tests/test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`** failed in the full run with an unraisable-exception error. It is fallout from a context leaked by the failed streaming session test, and it passes when run alone (4/4), so it isn't a separate bug.\n\nThe subagent's report had a small inconsistency: it counted 22 failures in group 1 but listed only 21 names. The 22nd is most likely `test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`, though the report doesn't say so explicitly.",
